VARIANT NAME KEY: fa = flash attention; Kq8 / Vq4 = K / V cache type q8_0 / q4_0; bN / ubN = batch / ubatch;
moeN = N MoE expert layers on the CPU (--n-cpu-moe); sdN<type> = speculative decoding with N draft tokens;
default = llama.cpp default batch sizes.

COLUMN KEY: pp_tps / tg_tps = prompt processing / token generation tokens per second (llama-bench: pp at the
largest prompt, tg of the first generation test; benchy: at the largest prompt, depth 0); *_std = standard
deviation over repetitions; ttft_ms = time to first token (benchy); vram_peak_mib = peak dedicated VRAM of the
GPU; server_shared_mib = peak shared GPU memory of the benchmark process (pinned host buffers for CPU experts
count here: that is NOT a spill); spill_mib = shared memory beyond what `llama-fit-params` expects (> ~100 MiB
= a real spill into system RAM); fit = llama-fit-params verdict before the run; status: ok | aborted (stopped by
the memory guard) | failed | skipped (did not fit, never started).

